---
const limitations = [
  {
    title: 'Active development',
    body: 'Bugs are still possible. Behavior, defaults, and edge cases will change. Always try on a copy of your library first.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Windows tested; long tracks',
    body: 'Tested on Windows by the author. Analysis and render load each file fully into memory; tracks longer than about 10 minutes may hang, use high RAM, or crash.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Pro-L 2 or LoudMax for limiter mode',
    body: 'Limiter-assisted processing requires either FabFilter Pro-L 2 (VST3) or LoudMax (free). Analysis and clean-gain render work without a limiter plugin.',
  },
  {
    title: 'UI still evolving',
    body: 'The app is functional but not polished. Expect rough edges while the interface improves.',
  },
];
---

<section class="section" id="limitations">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header reveal">
      <p class="section-label">Current limitations</p>
      <h2>What to expect right now</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        DropGain is a work in progress. A packaged Windows build is available; macOS and Linux may work from source but are untested.
        Validate results on a library copy before trusting a full batch.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card-grid card-grid-2">
      {
        limitations.map((item) => (
          <article class="glass-card limitation-card reveal">
            <h3>{item.title}</h3>
            <p class="text-muted">{item.body}</p>
          </article>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .limitation-card h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--fg-main);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .limitation-card p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }
</style>
